  "body": "[15:33]  <M-Matthew> also, how come i'm not allowed to invite you into it?\n[15:33]  <M-Erik> k\n[15:35]  <M-Erik> hmm, odd that you can't invite\n[15:36]  <M-Erik> I assume you were granted power before they up'd the invite level?\n[15:36]  <Ara4n> they didn't up the level though\n[15:36]  <Ara4n> you got in uninvited\n[15:37]  <M-Erik> Well, the invite level is set to 10\n[15:37]  <Ara4n> dave/kegan: **please** let's make sure that the react SDK actually displays all state changes in the timeline\n[15:37]  <Ara4n> so how did you manage to join?\n[15:37]  <M-Erik> because its a public room?\n[15:38]  <M-Dave> the client?\n[15:38]  <M-Erik> Why you would add an invite level to a public room is an interesting question, and is quite an unintuitive thing to do\n[15:42]  <Ara4n> if you do, it surely shouldn't stop you from inviting people given it's public\n[15:43]  <M-Erik> I guess we could special case it to ignore the invite rule if its public\n[15:43]  <Ara4n> doesn't seem unreasonable\n\n\n(Imported from https://matrix.org/jira/browse/SYN-410)\n\n(Reported by @ara4n)",
